# Folio Design System — Cursor Rules

You are working on the Folio Design System for the Cube platform.
Folio is an HTML/CSS design system that Claude and Cursor use to generate
on-brand UI screens. Read these rules before writing any code.

---

## Project Overview

Folio is a generative middle layer between design and code:

```
tokens.css + components/
        ↓
Generate ideation screens (HTML/CSS)
        ↓
Push to Figma via MCP
        ↓
Designers adjust in Figma
```

**Stack:** Vanilla HTML + CSS. No frameworks, no Tailwind, no React.
**Fonts:** DM Sans (body), Montserrat (display headings)
**Icons:** SVG registry in components/_sidebar-icons.js (data-icon pattern)

---

## Folder Structure

```
folio/
├── .cursorrules               ← you are here
├── CLAUDE.md                  ← Claude Code rules (same intent)
├── tokens.css                 ← single source of truth for all design tokens
├── components/
│   └── _sidebar-icons.js     ← SVG icon registry, auto-injects via data-icon
└── templates/
    └── shell.html             ← base shell for every screen
```

---

## Rule 1: Always start from the shell

Never rebuild the sidebar or top nav from scratch.
Copy `templates/shell.html` for every new screen.

To create a new screen:
1. Copy `templates/shell.html` → `templates/[screen-name].html`
2. Set the correct `.ni` to `class="ni active"`
3. Add page content inside `<main class="page-content">`
4. Add page-specific styles only — never redefine shell classes

---

## Rule 2: 4px spacing grid

Every spacing value — padding, margin, gap, height, width — must be
a multiple of 4px.

**Allowed:** 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 40, 48, 64
**Never use:** 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15 (or any non-multiple of 4)

Use spacing tokens from tokens.css:
```css
--spacing-1: 4px    --spacing-2: 8px    --spacing-3: 12px
--spacing-4: 16px   --spacing-5: 20px   --spacing-6: 24px
--spacing-8: 32px   --spacing-12: 48px
```

---

## Rule 3: Design tokens — always use exact values

Never approximate colors or invent values. Always reference tokens.css.

Key color values:
```
Primary blue:      #2667D8   (--color-blue-500)
Sidebar bg outer:  #F2F5F9
Card bg:           #FFFFFF
Border:            #E3E8EF
Text primary:      #222B3A
Text secondary:    #4A5567
Text muted:        #677489
Active nav bg:     #EFF6FF
Active nav border: #2667D8  (3px left stroke)
AI gradient:       linear-gradient(-19deg, #7A5AF8 33%, #9B8AFB 62%, #5925DC 98%)
```

---

## Rule 4: Icon system

All icons come from `components/_sidebar-icons.js`.
Use the `data-icon` attribute — never inline SVGs for sidebar icons.

```html
<!-- Correct -->
<div class="ni-ic" data-icon="home"></div>

<!-- Wrong — never do this -->
<svg>...</svg>
```

Available icons: home, cubeBI, reports, boards, smartVariance, aiAnalyst,
scenarios, workflows, library, dimensions, formulas, tags, integrations,
dataExport, users, currencies, auditTrail, aiPlugin, chatgpt, claude,
excel, sheets, slack, teams, powerpoint, slides, wordmark, logoMark,
collapseLeft, collapseRight

---

## Rule 5: Locked classes — never redefine

These classes are defined in shell.html and must not be overridden:

**Sidebar:**
`.sb`, `.sb-card`, `.sb-hdr`, `.sb-nav`, `.col-btn`,
`.dv`, `.nav-section`, `.sec`, `.ni`, `.ni.home`, `.ni.active`,
`.ni-ic`, `.ni-lbl`, `.apps-wrap`, `.apps-grid`, `.app-tile`,
`.app-circ`, `.app-lbl`

**Top nav:**
`.topnav`, `.tn-company`, `.tn-company-ic`, `.tn-company-name`,
`.tn-chevron`, `.tn-right`, `.tn-btn`, `.tn-ai-btn`, `.tn-ai-inner`,
`.tn-user`, `.tn-avatar`, `.tn-user-name`

**Shell:**
`.app-shell`, `.main`, `.page-content`

Only add NEW classes for page-specific content.

---

## Rule 6: Active nav state

Active nav items have:
- `background: #EFF6FF`
- `border-left: 3px solid #2667D8`
- `padding-left: 21px` (24px − 3px border)
- `width: calc(100% + 16px)` with `margin-left: -8px` to break out of section padding
- Label: `color: #2667D8`, `font-weight: 600`

Mark active by adding `class="ni active"` to the correct `.ni` element.

---

## Rule 7: Top nav structure

The top nav (`header.topnav`) has two fixed regions:

**Left — company selector:**
```html
<div class="tn-company">
  <div class="tn-company-ic"><!-- buildings SVG --></div>
  <span class="tn-company-name">Company Name</span>
  <div class="tn-chevron"><!-- chevron SVG --></div>
</div>
```

**Right — actions + user:**
```html
<div class="tn-right">
  <button class="tn-btn"><!-- icon --></button>    <!-- bg tasks -->
  <button class="tn-btn"><!-- icon --></button>    <!-- help -->
  <button class="tn-ai-btn">
    <div class="tn-ai-inner"><!-- sparkle --></div>
  </button>
  <div class="tn-user">
    <div class="tn-avatar">XX</div>               <!-- initials -->
    <span class="tn-user-name">Name</span>
    <div class="tn-chevron"><!-- chevron SVG --></div>
  </div>
</div>
```

---

## Rule 8: Page content area

All page-specific content goes inside:
```html
<main class="page-content">
  <!-- your content here -->
</main>
```

The `.page-content` class provides:
- `background: #FCFCFD`
- `padding: 32px`
- `overflow-y: auto`

---

## What NOT to do

- Do not use Tailwind classes
- Do not use React, Vue, or any framework
- Do not use Font Awesome CDN (icons come from _sidebar-icons.js)
- Do not rebuild the sidebar or top nav
- Do not use non-4px spacing values
- Do not hardcode colors — reference tokens.css values
- Do not add `!important` overrides
- Do not create new files unless the user asks
